WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
Winter on the coast of
Northern Ireland: green fields,

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.450
and mild air.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.730
Follow the same line around
the globe, far inland,

4
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.090
and winter can be a frozen, snowy plain.

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.250
This is climate, not a cold snap: the
average weather over a long period,

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.210
usually 30 years.

7
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.130
So why can two places the same distance
from the equator feel so different?

8
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.010
Is it the time zone?

9
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.890
Is the west always colder?

10
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.390
In this mission, you'll test, one by one,

11
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.930
the factors that shape a climate.

12
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.030
Then you'll put them together to
explain Northern Ireland's own climate.

13
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:42.050
Your mission: explain why places the same
distance from the equator can have different

14
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.000
climates.
